# Build-time configuration for the deployed frontend.
#
# Committed on purpose, which is worth justifying rather than assuming.
# Every value here is compiled into the client JavaScript bundle by Vite
# and shipped to every visitor, so none of it can be secret: a "secret"
# in this file would be a secret published on your own website. Firebase's
# web config is public by design -- access is controlled by Firebase
# Security Rules and the Authorized domains list, not by hiding the
# apiKey. Anything that genuinely must stay private (LLM keys, the
# Firebase *service account*, Razorpay's secret) belongs on the backend
# as a Render environment variable and must never become a VITE_ one.
# See docs/CONFIGURATION.md.
#
# This file exists so the deployment does not depend on a dashboard
# field being filled in correctly. Real environment variables still take
# precedence over it, so setting any of these as Cloudflare build
# variables later overrides what is here without editing this file --
# checked against Vite's loadEnv rather than assumed.
#
# frontend-react/.env (git-ignored) remains the local-development file
# and is unaffected by this one.

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSyDGhBvxUQK8x7h6EgYkzduo39M1dL-nlAM
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=ai-resume-builder-f5c47.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=ai-resume-builder-f5c47
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:600784500705:web:5a05cdc5001a7eb17644a0

# TODO: the deployed backend's origin, e.g. https://<service>.onrender.com
# -- no trailing slash, since lib/api.js concatenates paths directly onto
# it. While this is empty the frontend issues API calls at its own origin,
# where they 404 against the static assets and never reach the backend:
# sign-in itself still works (Firebase is contacted directly by the
# browser), but /auth/me and /history do not.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# TODO: the deployed site's own origin, e.g. https://ats-resume.<subdomain>.workers.dev
# Canonical URLs, og:url and sitemap.xml all derive from it; leaving it
# empty stamps every page with the placeholder domain
# resume-optimizer.example.com. See docs/SEO.md.
VITE_SITE_URL=
